      "message": "If we are intended to use the same variation name for the \u0027required\u0027 modules with \u0027image\u0027 variations, you may use `vendorImageVariant` and `productImageVariant` here.\nOr define `requiredModuleProductVariation :\u003d productImageVariant` to avoid hard coded names.\n\nAlso, as you commented, vendor and product variants have version suffix for the variant name. `required: [\"a{.vendor}\"]` means `a.vendor.{VER}`, `{VER}` is from the VndkVersion property from this module.\n\n`android/required.go` does not know this information. Maybe we need some more interface for the version suffix?",
